{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"The streamed tests pass with the race detector. I found a diagnostic regression: when a streamed patch read fails, the change-set path no longer adds Git’s stderr to the reported error. That leaves failures such as missing objects reported only as `exit status 128`. I’m checking the gate results before finalizing the review.\n"}}
